  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The three charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;are placed at the corners <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> of a square of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in figure. The magnitude of electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;at the corner <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of the square, is&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0118_b685159c24d3.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 152px;\" /></p>"
  },
